WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.060
If microglia eat retinal inputs, can we catch them doing it?

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.000
And do they choose what they eat?

3
00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:14.513
In 2012, Dorothy Schafer, in the Stevens laboratory, set out to look.

4
00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:18.943
Each eye got its own colored tracer at postnatal day four.

5
00:00:19.763 --> 00:00:22.023
A day later, they looked in the visual thalamus.

6
00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:26.693
A speck beside a microglial cell does not show it was eaten.

7
00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.393
So only label inside the cell counts.

8
00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:36.137
Retinal material sat inside microglial lysosomes, the cell's digestive compartments.

9
00:00:36.897 --> 00:00:38.857
A dye that glows only in acid agreed.

10
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:43.827
The swallowed material was mainly presynaptic, from retinal terminals.

11
00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:49.507
Eating had a clock.

12
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.967
It was high at postnatal day five, and much lower by day nine.

13
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.270
Eating also used a tag and a reader.

14
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:03.550
Without complement receptor 3, the reader, or C3, the tag's source, microglia took

15
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.570
up about half as much.

16
00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:10.393
Those mice later had more overlap between the eye territories, and extra retinal

17
00:01:10.393 --> 00:01:11.393
synapses.

18
00:01:11.966 --> 00:01:13.466
But half the eating remained.

19
00:01:14.386 --> 00:01:15.926
Complement is one route of several.

20
00:01:17.016 --> 00:01:18.296
Now the key question.

21
00:01:18.296 --> 00:01:22.796
Silence one eye with tetrodotoxin, which blocks sodium channels.

22
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:29.410
Predict. If microglia remove less active inputs, whose material should they hold

23
00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.410
more of?

24
00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:40.813
More of the silenced eye's material, relative to how much of that eye's input is

25
00:01:40.813 --> 00:01:41.813
there.

26
00:01:42.016 --> 00:01:46.656
Boost one eye with forskolin instead, and they take relatively more of the untreated

27
00:01:46.656 --> 00:01:47.656
eye's.

28
00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.500
The two drugs push in opposite directions.

29
00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.740
A drug that simply damaged axons would raise eating of its own eye both times.

30
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.870
Why relative to what is there?

31
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:06.930
Near one microglial cell, one eye's input can far outnumber the other's.

32
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.960
Say 90 units from one eye, and 10 from the other.

33
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.640
An eater with no preference takes a tenth of each, so it holds 9 to 1.

34
00:02:16.633 --> 00:02:21.393
Now silence the minor eye, and let the eater take twice the fraction of it: two

35
00:02:21.393 --> 00:02:22.793
tenths instead of one tenth.

36
00:02:23.633 --> 00:02:25.913
It holds 2 units, still fewer than 9.

37
00:02:26.916 --> 00:02:31.676
So a fair test compares each eye with its own input, measured where the microglia

38
00:02:31.676 --> 00:02:32.676
are sampled.

39
00:02:33.316 --> 00:02:37.696
Now the limits. This compares whole eyes, not single synapses.

40
00:02:38.656 --> 00:02:40.976
It does not show how activity becomes a mark.

41
00:02:41.856 --> 00:02:46.796
And later imaging elsewhere suggests microglia often take bites, not whole synapses.

42
00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.380
Here is the idea again.

43
00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.600
Relative activity biases how much material microglia take from each eye.

44
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.260
Complement helps them take part of it.

45
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.340
How the two connect is still open.
